                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Neat!\n\nIt's obviously a mobile game and a clone of you-know-what, but it's pretty good for its genre. Levels, towers, upgrades (both in-level and global), extra abilities (cooldown-based), environment hazards (some work for you, some against you) - all the pieces of a good tower defence game are there.\n\nOne issue I would point out is that there's no option to setup target priority for the towers - they always shoot the first mob on the line, which is often not the most optimal target, e.g. a magic-damage tower shooting a magic-resisting target.",
